            "intro": "Hy-Tech Engineers IPO | This fund raising via anchor book was ahead of its IPO opening for the public which is scheduled on August 24 and closing on August 27.",
            "body": "Maharashtra-based Hy-Tech Engineers, which manufactures hydraulic fittings and forged components for industrial applications, has raised Rs 40.72 crore from eight anchor investors ahead of the opening of its initial public offering (IPO).\r\n\r\nWhiteOak Capital Asset Management, part of the White Oak Capital Group founded by veteran investor Prashant Khemka, emerged as the largest anchor investor, accounting for 43 percent of the total allocation.\r\n\r\nThe IPO will open for public subscription on August 24 and close on August 27. The company is looking to raise Rs 135.7 crore through the issue at the upper end of the price band of Rs 50-53 per share.\r\n\r\nThe IPO comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 60 crore and an offer for sale (OFS) of 1.42 crore equity shares worth Rs 75.73 crore at the upper end of the price band.\r\n\r\nHy-Tech Engineers said it has allotted 76.83 lakh shares to anchor investors at Rs 53 per share.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\n&amp;nbsp;\r\n\r\nWhiteOak Capital leads anchor allocation\r\n\r\nWhiteOak Capital Asset Management bought 33.43 lakh shares worth Rs 17.72 crore, making it the biggest investor in the anchor book.\r\n\r\nWinro Commercial (India), owned by the Ashwin Kumar Kothari group, picked up 22.64 lakh shares worth Rs 11.99 crore.\r\n\r\nAshika Global Finance bought 11.32 lakh shares worth Rs 6 crore, while Varanium Emerging Fund acquired 9.43 lakh shares for Rs 5 crore.\r\n\r\nHow Hy-Tech Engineers plans to use IPO proceeds\r\n\r\nThe company plans to use Rs 29.9 crore of the net fresh issue proceeds to procure machinery and equipment for capacity expansion at its Kavathe, Shirwal and Pithampur facilities.\r\n\r\nAnother Rs 16 crore will be used to repay debt, with the remaining proceeds earmarked for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nManufacturing capacity, financial performance\r\n\r\nHy-Tech Engineers operates six manufacturing facilities across Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh.\r\n\r\nAs of March 2026, the company had a combined annual installed capacity of 4.83 crore hydraulic fittings and 3,120 metric tonnes per annum (MTPA) of forging capacity.\r\n\r\nThe company reported a 15.15 percent year-on-year increase in profit to Rs 22.6 crore in FY26, while revenue from operations rose 17.4 percent to Rs 189.4 crore.\r\n\r\nThe merchant banker for managing the Hy-Tech Engineers IPO is New Berry Capitals.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/hy-tech-engineers-ipo-anchor-investors-pick-up-rs-40-7-crore-worth-of-shares-whiteoak-capital-takes-43-of-the-book-14012613.html",
