          "1": {
            "id": "14012598",
            "headline": "Symbiotec Pharmalab raises over Rs 526 crore from 34 anchor investors ahead of Rs 1,757-crore IPO",
            "heading": "Symbiotec Pharmalab raises over Rs 526 crore from 34 anchor investors ahead of Rs 1,757-crore IPO",
            "intro": "Symbiotec Pharmalab IPO | The company will open its IPO for the public subscription on August 24 and close on August 27, while the price band for the offer has been fixed at Rs 938-988 per share.",
            "body": "Madhya Pradesh-based contract development and manufacturing organisation (CDMO) Symbiotec Pharmalab has raised Rs 526.2 crore through its anchor book, a day ahead of the opening of its Rs 1,757-crore initial public offering (IPO).\r\n\r\nThe company will open its IPO for public subscription on August 24 and close on August 27. The price band has been fixed at Rs 938-988 per share.\r\n\r\nThe IPO comprises a fresh issue of shares worth Rs 150 crore and an offer for sale (OFS) of Rs 1,607 crore. Promoter Satwani Holdings and promoters Rosewood Investments and Motilal Oswal are the selling shareholders in the OFS.\r\n\r\nSymbiotec Pharmalab\u00a0said it has allocated 53.25 lakh equity shares to 34 anchor investors at Rs 988 per share. The investors include Citigroup Global Markets, BNP Paribas, Singularity AMC, backed by Madhusudan Kela, Susquehanna Pacific and TIMF Holdings.\r\n\r\nEleven domestic mutual funds, including ICICI Prudential AMC, HDFC Mutual Fund, Motilal Oswal AMC, Mirae Asset, Tata Mutual Fund, Edelweiss, Groww Mutual Fund and ITI Mutual Fund, picked up 31.98 lakh shares through 19 schemes.\r\n\r\nInsurance companies Tata AIA Life, Bajaj Life and Bharti AXA Life also bought 4.25 lakh shares worth Rs 42 crore.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nHow Symbiotec Pharmalab plans to use IPO proceeds\r\n\r\nThe Rosewood Investments and Motilal Oswal-backed company plans to use Rs 112.5 crore from the net fresh issue proceeds to repay debt. The remaining fresh issue proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nProceeds from the OFS will accrue to the selling shareholders.\r\n\r\nSymbiotec Pharmalab operates as a CDMO for specialty pharmaceutical and nutraceutical companies globally. Its operations are built around three platforms \u2014 organic chemistry, biotechnology and complex injectables.\r\n\r\nManufacturing capacity\r\n\r\nAs of March 2026, the company had two operational industrial-scale active pharmaceutical ingredient (API) manufacturing facilities with a maximum chemical synthesis capacity of 584.67 metric tonnes (MT) and fermentation capacity of 300 kilolitres (KL).\r\n\r\nIt has also commissioned two additional manufacturing facilities at Ujjain and Mhow in Madhya Pradesh.\r\n\r\nThe company is expanding its biologics capacity and has proposed adding a dedicated 14 KL fermentation facility for biologics manufacturing at Ujjain.\r\n\r\nFinancial performance\r\n\r\nSymbiotec Pharmalab\u2019s profit grew at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 4.81 percent to Rs 109.9 crore in FY26 from FY24.\r\n\r\nRevenue increased at a CAGR of 10.16 percent during the same period to Rs 869.1 crore.\r\n\r\nJM Financial, Avendus Capital, Motilal Oswal Investment Advisors and Nomura Financial Advisory and Securities (India) are acting as the book-running lead managers for the\u00a0Symbiotec Pharmalab IPO.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/symbiotec-pharmalab-raises-over-rs-526-crore-from-34-anchor-investors-ahead-of-rs-1-757-crore-ipo-14012598.html",
