            "headline": "Skyways Air Services raises over Rs 174 crore via anchor book, Rs 583-crore IPO to open on August 24",
            "heading": "Skyways Air Services raises over Rs 174 crore via anchor book, Rs 583-crore IPO to open on August 24",
            "intro": "Skyways Air Services IPO | The company intends to spend Rs 216.8 crore of net fresh issue proceeds for repaying debt against the total outstanding borrowings of Rs 586.2 crore as of June 2026.",
            "body": "Delhi-based air freight forwarder Skyways Air Services has raised Rs 174.5 crore through its anchor book, a day ahead of the opening of its initial public offering (IPO) for public subscription.\r\n\r\nThe company is looking to raise up to Rs 582.8 crore through the IPO by issuing 4.22 crore equity shares at the upper end of the price band of Rs 131-138 per share.\r\n\r\nThe IPO comprises a fresh issue of 2.88 crore equity shares and an offer for sale (OFS) of 1.33 crore shares. The issue will open for public subscription on August 24 and close on August 27.\r\n\r\nSkyways Air Services IPO details said it has allocated 1.26 crore equity shares to 17 anchor investors at Rs 138 per share. The anchor investors include Nomura Singapore, Citigroup, LC Pharos Multi Strategy Fund, Holani Venture Capital Fund, Pranitya India Opportunities Fund and IndusInd General Insurance.\r\n\r\nOf the total anchor allocation, 50.5 lakh shares worth Rs 69.69 crore were allotted to two domestic mutual funds \u2014 Bank of India Mutual Fund and Taurus Asset Management \u2014 through six schemes, according to the company's filing.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nSkyways Air Services\u00a0intends to spend Rs 216.8 crore of net fresh issue proceeds for repaying debt against the total outstanding borrowings of Rs 586.2 crore as of June 2026.\r\n\r\nFurther, Rs 130 crore will be utilised for its incremental working capital requirements, and the remaining amount for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nThe financial performance of the company has been strong in the recent past years with the profit soaring 32 percent to Rs 63.5 crore in the fiscal year ended March 2026 from Rs 48.1 crore in previous year. Revenue during the same periods grew by 25.1 percent to Rs 2,812.9 crore from Rs 2,247.8 crore.\r\n\r\nHolani Consultants, Shannon Advisors, and Dolat Finserv are acting as the merchant bankers for the\u00a0Skyways Air Services IPO.",
